From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Taylor <zctaylor.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:30:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/30] Let microVM worker pools give actors /dev/fuse

A microVM actor cannot mount a FUSE filesystem. The guest kernel has
fuse and the actor can hold SYS_ADMIN, but the guest container has no
/dev/fuse, the actor cannot mknod it, and the spec has no device field.

Add guestDevices to a WorkerPool sandbox class, an allowlist that holds
only "fuse". The CRD refuses it on any class but microvm. The controller
passes it to ateworker-microvm as --guest-devices, only when set. The
worker adds each node to linux.devices with a device cgroup allow rule
after the default deny. The kata spec converter now forwards
linux.devices, so the agent creates the node in the guest container's
/dev. The guest kernel serves the device, so the actor gets no host
device.

An actor reaches such a pool through a pool label and the template's
workerSelector, and it still needs SYS_ADMIN to mount.

The e2e probe gets a /fuse endpoint that mounts a FUSE filesystem it
serves itself. The guestdevices suite resumes an actor on a pool with and
without guestDevices, and checks that the API server refuses the field
on a gvisor class.

Fork-Topic: microvm-fuse
Fork-Upstream: candidate
